---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';

/**
 * Safety, community rules and child protection EN, mirror of
 * cs/bezpecnost.astro. Czech version is authoritative.
 */

const lastUpdated = '2026-10-17';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Safety and Child Protection"
  description="Melveo community rules, how to report inappropriate content and how we protect children and young athletes."
  lang="en"
>
  <PageHeader lang="en" />
  <article class="legal-article">
    <p class="legal-eyebrow">Effective · {lastUpdated}</p>
    <h1 class="legal-h1">Safety and Child Protection</h1>
    <p class="legal-lead">
      Melveo is used by clubs and teams, many of them youth teams. Content in
      the app is visible only to members of the team the club invited them
      to, according to their role. This page explains what does not belong in
      the app, how to report content and how we protect children.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>1. Community rules</h2>
    <p>The following does not belong in Melveo:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>insults, ridicule, bullying and harassment,</li>
      <li>sexual content and anything that sexualises minors,</li>
      <li>violence, threats and incitement to hatred,</li>
      <li>publishing other people's personal or health data without authorisation,</li>
      <li>spam and content unrelated to sports preparation.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The rules apply to names and nicknames, team names and logos, notes,
      training plans, measurement results, videos, clips and commentary.
    </p>

    <h2>2. How to report content</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>In the app:</strong> touch and hold the content (member
        name, team name, note, training plan, measurement note, commentary)
        and choose Report. For videos and clips, Report is in the top bar.
        Pick a reason and optionally add a note.</li>
      <li><strong>By email:</strong> at
        <a href="mailto:hello@melveo.app">hello@melveo.app</a>, even without
        an account in the app.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Reports go to Melveo support and to the team admins. Neither the admins
      nor the author of the content can see who reported it.
    </p>

    <h2>3. What happens after a report</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We reply within 24 hours on working days.</li>
      <li>Reports with the reason Danger to minors are handled first.</li>
      <li>Content that breaks these rules or the law is removed, and depending
        on severity we restrict or end its author's access.</li>
      <li>A team admin can remove a member from the team at any time.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Child protection</h2>
    <p>
      Melveo does not tolerate any form of child abuse or endangerment.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>For players under 15, the club obtains the consent of a parent or
        legal guardian to the processing of their data (Section 7 of Czech
        Act No. 110/2019 Coll.). When joining a team, the player enters their
        year of birth and confirms that the club has this consent. A team
        admin confirms it for the club in the team settings.</li>
      <li>Team content is visible only to team members according to their
        role. The app has no public profiles and no messaging between
        strangers.</li>
      <li>We pass any suspicion of child abuse to the Police of the Czech
        Republic and other competent authorities and cooperate with them.</li>
      <li>In immediate danger, call 158 or 112. Children and young people can
        call the Czech helpline Linka bezpečí at 116 111.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="legal-block">
      Child protection contact:
      <a href="mailto:hello@melveo.app?subject=Child%20protection">hello@melveo.app</a>,
      subject Child protection.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Operator</h2>
    <p class="legal-block">
      <strong>QUIX Global s.r.o.</strong>, Company ID 22466444,
      Příčná 1892/4, Nové Město, 110 00 Prague 1, Czech Republic.
      More details in the <a href="/en/terms/">Terms</a> and the
      <a href="/en/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
